  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing visa management efficiency: integrated digital solutions for Costa Rica</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A 2023 IOM assessment of Costa Rica&apos;s Directorate General of Migration and Foreigners (DGME) identified significant challenges in visa processing and highlighted the potential of the Migration Information and Data Analysis System (MIDAS) to strengthen efficiency. This project aims to support sustainable and effective border governance in Costa Rica through the digitalization and modernization of visa procedures. First, a workload and gender-sensitive assessment of the DGME Visa Unit and Costa Rican consulates in Colombia and Nicaragua will identify operational bottlenecks and inform MIDAS customization needs (Output 1.1). Based on these findings, a customized MIDAS e-Visa module adapted to Costa Rica&apos;s operational context will be developed and made available (Output 1.2). DGME and consular officials will then receive technical guidance and IT support to build the skills required to implement and manage the new system effectively (Output 1.3). In parallel, communication channels between the DGME, consulates, and potential applicants, particularly women and marginalized groups, will be strengthened to improve access to information on visa categories and application procedures (Output 1.4). These interventions will enable the DGME and consulates to manage visa processes more efficiently through integrated digital solutions (Outcome 1).</narrative>
  </description>
